                    {
                        "sense_id": "b830459d-2cf0-3710-b0ac-aa1ecd31a318",
                        "entry_id": "e5b80dca-2dee-33dd-8486-362e0ea0e42a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Science des critères de jugement, de la connaissance de la vérité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7c163617-3fa7-4f75-aab9-5c355e463226",
                                "sense_id": "b830459d-2cf0-3710-b0ac-aa1ecd31a318",
                                "text": "La théodicée science rationnelle de Dieu en dehors de toute révélation. La logique qui formule les règles à suivre pour que l’esprit parvienne à la vérité et la critériologie qui expose les fondements de la certitude, les rapports entre le sujet connaissant et l’objet connu."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7b19a84-19aa-4493-a94f-8bc70bdf7396",
                                "sense_id": "b830459d-2cf0-3710-b0ac-aa1ecd31a318",
                                "text": "Le choix optimum des critères relève d'une réflexion méthodologique apparentée à la recherche opérationnelle : la critériologie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2715d9aa-8944-4acb-b99c-2d3f8ba4295a",
                        "source_entry_id": "e5b80dca-2dee-33dd-8486-362e0ea0e42a",
                        "source_sense_id": "b830459d-2cf0-3710-b0ac-aa1ecd31a318",
                        "target_lang_word": "criteriology",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "criteriology",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e2f61d0a-f646-3ada-9a76-7c1ce1f540f9",
                                        "entry_id": "724c39f0-4f9c-3801-8255-f9315323a14d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The study of the validity of reasoning and the criteria necessary to achieve knowledge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4723da75-59d1-483e-a720-63ee719788c4",
                                                "sense_id": "e2f61d0a-f646-3ada-9a76-7c1ce1f540f9",
                                                "text": "But it seems otherwise with reasoning as viewed by criteriology."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5a4abdfb-af2d-4699-83fe-00299e52dd61",
                                                "sense_id": "e2f61d0a-f646-3ada-9a76-7c1ce1f540f9",
                                                "text": "According to Mercier, criteriology should demonstrate the fallacy of two forms of scepticism: one that casts doubts on each of the acts of the human reason and one that casts doubts on the very possibility of arriving at a knowledge of the truth."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7830e5b-7594-4e23-b71a-758f454b5e2b",
                                                "sense_id": "e2f61d0a-f646-3ada-9a76-7c1ce1f540f9",
                                                "text": "In the other kind of knowledge, reflection develops a criteriology of the divine to judge whether or not consciousness is testifying to the true God or some phantasm of the divine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
